WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.670
I kind of understood Men in Black a

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:04.100
little bit, but I didn't want to make

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.420
Men in Black.

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:06.950
That was the next year after

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:07.970
Independence Day.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.770
So I didn't want to make two alien

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.070
movies back to back.

00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:12.080
How did he convince you?

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.990
Steven Spielberg sent a helicopter for

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:15.350
me.

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:17.830
You god damn liar.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:18.320
Yeah.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.400
I was in New York. To talk to you.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.720
To talk to me, to talk.

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.020
You like it landed at his house and he

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.040
had me at hello.

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:27.290
Well, yeah. You can't say no after you

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.520
get off the helicopter. Yeah, he

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:29.640
Get off the helicopter at his house.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.140
He says, Come on.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:30.470
What are you.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.180
And it was the first time I'd ever had

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.970
lemonade with carbonated water.

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:36.380
Yeah. You can't say no.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.490
You can't say no to that. There was

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:40.340
lemonade with carbonated water and--

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.300
But you had to act like you had it

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:41.510
before.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.370
Yeah, yeah, yeah. I was like, Yeah, this

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:43.940
is regular.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:44.510
That's good. Shit.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:45.830
Yeah. Is this carbonated water?

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:46.820
Just like my grandmother used.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:47.630
To make carbonated water?

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:48.320
I would say.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:49.520
That. Yeah. This is good shit, Steve.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.310
But, yeah, he. He flew me in and he, he,

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.050
he said the coldest shit.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:58.430
He said, he said tell me, tell me why

00:00:58.430 --> 00:01:01.100
you don't want to make my movie.

00:01:01.370 --> 00:01:04.520
And he was the producer and I was like

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.950
and he, he, he put the ellipses at the

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.030
end. It was the dot, dot, dot.

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.560
Tell me why you don't want to make my

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.000
movie. It was the dot, dot, dot.

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:12.980
If he had continued, he would have

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.440
said, Joker, you know, I made Jaws.

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.040
Right? Yeah. Or, you know, I.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:17.820
Made E.T..

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:18.690
Or Motherf*****.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:19.320
Motherf*****. He might have.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:20.550
Said. He might have said he's

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:21.900
respectful. Why don't you want to make

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:22.230
my movie?

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:23.100
Well, you don't want to make it.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.800
Like, a very low tone to it.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.360
And he. I walked in his house, and he

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:29.730
had the Jaws poster and the.

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:32.460
Was the, Jurassic Park.

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.890
He had everything. So it was just so I

00:01:34.890 --> 00:01:35.430
would know.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.030
What's your answer?

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:37.410
What's my answer? And I was like, you

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.480
know, I didn't want to make two alien

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.530
movies back to back.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.940
I didn't want to go from Independence

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.940
Day to Men in Black, you know, I felt

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.560
like I would I didn't want to be the

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.340
alien guy.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.560
But I mean, honestly, it's a it's a

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.380
worry that we have because I think the

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:54.720
the biggest thing that we think about

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.000
while having a moment at the top is,

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:58.650
well, how do you stay at the top?

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.240
And I don't want to make mistakes.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.740
I definitely don't want to keep doing

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:02.730
the right thing. I don't want him to

00:02:02.730 --> 00:02:03.900
think that this is the only thing I can

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.730
do. I want to expand and do more.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:07.590
So I understand that logic.

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.180
I understand why it would be worried.

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.640
I mean, for him, it's just basically

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.380
like, I'm Steven Spielberg and you're

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.570
protected. Yeah. Don't make bad stuff.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:15.870
Yeah.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.760
And that goes back to one of the one of

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.200
the earlier questions.

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:22.480
It's like. It's a team sport.

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.960
You know, and.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:28.070
The there's a couple of really critical

00:02:28.070 --> 00:02:30.440
things. It's like, who is at your right

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:33.590
hand? Like who your friends are, who

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.770
you're with every day will make or

00:02:36.770 --> 00:02:38.370
break your dreams.

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:43.340
You cannot build a career.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:47.150
And you probably you know, I'm going to

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:48.800
speak specifically from my experience,

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.720
but you probably can't do much of

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:53.990
anything in this life at a high level

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:55.610
without a rock solid team.

00:02:55.610 --> 00:02:58.520
And in your in your rise of it.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.800
Did you see that or were you the

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:02.480
individual that felt you were doing it

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:03.470
by yourself?

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.930
Now. I never I never really thought I

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:06.980
was doing it by myself.

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:09.200
I knew that I had to be the tip of the

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.510
spear in terms of discipline.

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:12.980
I knew I had to be the tip of the spear

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.170
in terms of direction.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:19.940
But but I always knew that I needed my

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.040
squad. You know, we've talked a lot

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.650
about, you know, our our parents.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:26.480
Absolutely. And, you know, my father

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.450
was military. So it was very clear to

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:31.220
me that there was a commander.

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:32.900
So the commander is in charge.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.400
But if you ain't got nothing to

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.800
command, nobody is willing to follow

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:37.670
you. You got nothing.

